hadiths[202]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20053","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Qatadah narrated to us, and Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, Sa'id informed us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, and a man behind him recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. When he prayed, he said: Which of you recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man said: I did. He said: I knew that one of you distracted me from it."
"20054","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah who said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa narrate from Imran ibn Husayn, and he mentioned the like of it."
"20055","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Rabah who said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar, he said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"20056","Waki' narrated to us, Khalid ibn Rabah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar, he said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20057","Waki' narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: I had a fistula, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer. He said: Pray standing, if you cannot, then sitting, if you cannot, then on your side."
"20058","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, Hilal ibn Yasaf narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who grow fat, loving fatness, giving testimony before they are asked for it."
"20059","Waki' narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The begging of a rich man is a disgrace on his face on the Day of Resurrection. My father said: I do not know anyone who narrated it with a chain except Waki'."
"20060","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn Husayn who said, Abd al-Rahman said: A group from Banu Tamim came, Waki' said: Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Rejoice, O Banu Tamim. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave us glad tidings, so give us. Abd al-Rahman said: The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed. He said: A tribe from Yemen came, and he said: Accept the glad tidings, since Banu Tamim did not accept them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we accept."
"20061","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of this ummah are the generation among whom I was sent, Abd al-Samad said: those among whom I was sent, then those who follow them. Then there will arise a people who vow but do not fulfill, betray and are not trusted, bear witness though not asked, and fatness will appear among them."
"20062","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Miraya, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah, the Blessed and Exalted."
"20063","Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so does not break fast in the daytime all his life. He said: He neither broke fast nor fasted."
"20064","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, having no wealth besides them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for them, divided them into thirds, then cast lots among them, freed two and enslaved four, and said severe words to him."
"20065","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed two men of the Muslims for a man of the polytheists from Banu Uqayl."
"20066","Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salutation in three rak'ahs of Asr, then stood and entered. A man called al-Khirbaq, who had long hands, stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah. He came out to him, and he mentioned to him what he had done. He came and said: Is this one truthful? They said: Yes. He prayed the rak'ah he had left, then gave salutation, then prostrated two prostrations, then gave salutation."
"20067","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Zurarah ibn Awfa, Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: Ya'la ibn Munyah, or Ibn Umayyah, fought a man, and one of them bit the hand of his companion, and he pulled his hand from his mouth, knocking out his front tooth, and Hajjaj said: his two front teeth. They disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Does one of you bite his brother as the stallion bites? There is no blood money for it."
"20068","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah who said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi narrate that he heard Imran ibn Husayn al-Khuza'i narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Modesty brings only good. Bushayr ibn Ka'b said: It is written in wisdom that part of it is dignity and part of it is calmness. Imran said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you narrate to me from your pages."
"20069","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us cauterization, but we were cauterized and did not prosper nor succeed."
"20070","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah who said: I heard Abu Miraya al-Ijli, he said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"20071","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal who said: I heard Mutarrif say: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: I will narrate to you a hadith by which Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, may benefit you: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah, then did not forbid it until he died, and no Quran was revealed forbidding it."
"20072","And he used to greet me, but when I was cauterized he stopped, and when I left it he returned to me."
"20073","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed us, from Yazid al-Rishk who said: I heard Mutarrif narrate from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked, or it was said to him: Are the people of the Fire distinguished from the people of Paradise? He said: Yes. He said: Why then do workers work? He said: Each works for what he was created for, or for what was made easy for him."
"20074","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj informed us, Shu'bah informed us, he said: I heard Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Zahdam ibn Mudarrib, Hajjaj said in his hadith, he said: Zahdam came to me in my house and narrated to me, he said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Imran said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said after his generation twice or three times. Then there will be after them a people who bear witness though not asked, betray and are not trusted, vow but do not fulfill, and fatness will appear among them."
"20075","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, he said: I heard Abu Jamrah say: Zahdam came to me in my house and narrated to me, he said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are my generation, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: And they betray and are not trusted."
"20076","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah who said: I heard Mutarrif narrate that he had two wives. He said: He came to one of them, and she began pulling his turban, saying: You came from your other wife. He said: I came from Imran ibn Husayn, and he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I think he said: The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women."
"20077","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah who said: I heard a man from Banu Layth say: I bear witness concerning Imran ibn Husayn, Shu'bah said: Or Imran said: I bear witness concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade green glazed jars, or he said: hantam jars, and gold rings, and silk."
"20078","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from the nephew of Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir who said: I heard Mutarrif narrate from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you fast anything from the sirar of this month, meaning Sha'ban? He said: No. He said to him: When you break fast from Ramadan, fast a day or two days, the one who doubted doubted about it. He said: And I think he said: two days."
"20079","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, and Abd al-Wahhab, from a companion of his, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, that he said: I was with Imran ibn Husayn in Kufah, and Ali ibn Abi Talib led us in prayer, saying takbir whenever he prostrated and whenever he raised his head. When he finished, Imran said: This one led us in a prayer like the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20080","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah who said: Imran ibn Husayn sent for me in his illness, so I came to him. He said to me: I used to narrate to you hadiths by which Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, may benefit you after me. Know that he used to greet me. If I live, conceal from me, and if I die, narrate if you wish."
"20081","And know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah, then no book was revealed concerning it, nor did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it. A man said concerning it by his opinion what he wished."
"20082","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif who said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me, and he mentioned the like of it, and said: Do not narrate them until I die."
"20083","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Sa'id narrated to us, and Yazid informed us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit a man on his forearm, Ibn Numayr said: He pulled his hand from him and his two front teeth fell out, so he pulled it and his front tooth was uprooted. That was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he invalidated it and said: Did you intend to chew the flesh of your brother as the stallion chews."
"20084","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that Hayyaj ibn Imran came to Imran ibn Husayn and said: My father vowed that if he could overpower his slave, he would cut off a piece of him, or cut off his hand. He said: Tell your father to expiate his oath and not cut a piece of him, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation. Then he came to Samurah ibn Jundub and said the like of that to him."
"20085","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man from the Ansar freed six slaves at his death, having no wealth besides them. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he spoke severely to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for them, cast lots among them, freed two and returned four to slavery."
"20086","Bahz and Affan, in meaning, narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, Affan said: Al-Hasan narrated to them, from Hayyaj ibn Imran al-Burjumi, that a slave of his father fled, and he made it binding upon himself for Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, that if he could overpower him, he would cut off his hand. He said: He overpowered him. He said: He sent me to Imran ibn Husayn. He said: He said: Convey peace to your father and inform him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation, so let him expiate his oath and pardon his slave. He said: And he sent me to Samurah, and he said: Convey peace to your father and inform him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation, so let him expiate his oath and pardon his slave."
"20087","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj, he mentioned its meaning."
"20088","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son died, what is my share of his inheritance? He said: For you is a sixth. When he turned away, he called him and said: For you is another sixth. When he turned away, he called him and said: The other sixth is an extra provision."
"20089","Bahz narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, or from Imran ibn Husayn, that he said: I bear witness concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade us wearing silk and drinking from green glazed jars."
"20090","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, in meaning, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif who said: Imran ibn Husayn said: We performed tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Quran was revealed concerning it, Affan said: And the Quran descended concerning it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without forbidding it, and nothing abrogated it. A man said by his opinion what he wished."
"20091","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will remain a group of my ummah upon the truth, victorious over those who oppose them, until the command of Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, comes and Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, descends."
"20092","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women, and I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor."
"20093","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Salm ibn Zarir narrated to us, Abu Raja narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked, and he mentioned the like of it."
"20094","al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20095","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Qaza'ah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, nor janab, nor shighar."
"20096","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a Muslim woman was captured by the enemy, and they had earlier taken a she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: She saw heedlessness from the people, so she mounted the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then vowed to slaughter it. She arrived at Madinah and wanted to slaughter the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but she was prevented from that. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What a bad reward you gave it. Then he said: There is no vow for the son of Adam in what he does not own, nor in disobedience to Allah, the Blessed and Exalted."
"20097","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never stood among us as a preacher except that he commanded us with charity and forbade us mutilation. He said: And he said: Indeed among mutilation is for a man to vow to slit his nose. Indeed among mutilation is for a man to vow to perform Hajj walking, so let him offer a sacrificial animal and ride."
"20098","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us with a sermon except that he commanded us with charity and forbade us mutilation."
"20099","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: A woman cursed a she-camel of hers, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is cursed, so leave it alone. He said: I saw it following the dwellings, with no one confronting it, a grey she-camel."
"20100","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah and more than one, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir who said: I and Imran ibn Husayn prayed in Kufah behind Ali ibn Abi Talib, and he said takbir with us, this takbir when bowing and when prostrating, all of it. When we finished, Imran said to me: I have not prayed for a while, or he said: for such-and-such, a prayer more resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this prayer, meaning the prayer of Ali, may Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with him."
"20101","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman from Juhaynah confessed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of adultery and said: I am pregnant. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well, and when she gives birth then inform me. He did so, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding her, so her clothes were tied over her, then he ordered her stoning, so she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, you stoned her then you pray over her? He said: She has repented a repentance which, if divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, would encompass them. And have you found anything better than that she gave herself generously for Allah, Blessed and Exalted?"
"20102","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man bit a man and his front tooth was knocked out, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nullified it and said: You wanted to crunch your brother's hand as the stallion crunches."
"20103","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Al-Adba belonged to a man from Banu Uqayl and was among the foremost camels of the pilgrims. The man was captured and al-Adba was taken with him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he was in bonds, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a donkey with a velvet cloth over it. He said: O Muhammad, you take me and take the foremost camel of the pilgrims? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We take you for the crime of your allies Thaqif. He said: Thaqif had captured two men from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said in what he said: And I am a Muslim. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you had said it while you controlled your affair, you would have prospered with complete prosperity. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on. He said: He said: O Muhammad, I am hungry, so feed me, and I am thirsty, so give me drink. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is your need. Then he was ransomed for the two men, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept al-Adba for his own riding. He said: Then the polytheists raided the pasturing camels of Madinah and took them, and al-Adba was among them. He said: And they captured a woman from the Muslims. He said: When they camped they rested their camels in their courtyards. He said: The woman got up one night after they were made to sleep, and whenever she came to a camel it growled until she came to al-Adba, and she came to a trained docile she-camel with a bell, so she rode it, then directed it toward Madinah. He said: And she vowed that if Allah, Mighty and Majestic, saved her on it, she would slaughter it. When she reached Madinah the she-camel was recognized, and it was said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of her vow, or she came to him and informed him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil is what she rewarded it, or: evil is what you rewarded it, if Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saved her on it she would slaughter it. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in what the son of Adam does not own. And Wuhayb, meaning Ibn Khalid, said: Thaqif were allies of Banu Uqayl. And Hammad ibn Salamah added in it: Al-Adba was a household camel not kept from a basin or pasture. Affan said: Mujarrasah means trained."
"20104","Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, so we were cauterized, but we did not prosper nor succeed."
"20105","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Nadrah, that a youth asked Imran ibn Husayn about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while traveling, so he turned to the gathering of al-Uqah and said: This youth asked me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while traveling, so retain from me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never traveled a journey except that he prayed two rakahs, two rakahs, until he returned. And he stayed in Makkah at the time of the Conquest eighteen nights, praying with the people two rakahs, two rakahs."
"20106","My father said, and Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated it to us with this chain and added in it: except Maghrib. Then he would say: O people of Makkah, stand and pray two other rakahs, for we are travelers. Then he raided Hunayn and al-Taif and prayed two rakahs, two rakahs. Then he returned to Jiranah and performed Umrah from it in Dhu al-Qadah. Then I raided with Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and I performed Hajj and Umrah, and he prayed two rakahs, two rakahs. And with Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and he prayed two rakahs, two rakahs. Yunus said: except Maghrib. And with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, in the beginning of his rule, Yunus said: two rakahs except Maghrib. Then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, after that prayed four."
"20107","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man from the Ansar freed six slaves of his at his death, and he had no wealth other than them. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: I had intended not to pray over him. He said: Then he called for the slaves and divided them into three parts, so he freed two and kept four in slavery."
"20108","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him. So he stood and lined us behind him, and I was in the second row, and he prayed over him."
"20109","Mutamir narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed three rakahs then gave salam, so it was said to him, so he stood and prayed a rakah then gave salam, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting."
"20110","Ismail narrated to us, Yazid, meaning al-Rishk, narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of Hell? He said: Yes. He said: Then for what do workers work? He said: Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for, or as he said."
"20111","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys, and a woman from the Ansar was on a she-camel, it became difficult, so she cursed it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and said: Take what is on it and leave it, for it is cursed. Imran said: It is as if I look at it now walking among the people, no one turning to it, meaning the she-camel."
"20112","Ismail narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd said, from Abu Nadrah, who said: Imran ibn Husayn passed by, so we sat. A youth from the people stood to him and asked him about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in battle, Hajj and Umrah. So he came and stood over us and said: This one asked me about a matter, and I wanted you to hear it, or as he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed only two rakahs until he returned to Madinah. And I performed Hajj with him, and he prayed only two rakahs until he returned to Madinah. And I witnessed with him the Conquest, so he stayed in Makkah eighteen, praying only two rakahs, and saying to the people of the town: Pray four, for we are travelers. And I performed with him three Umrahs, and he prayed only two rakahs. And I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, several pilgrimages, and they prayed only two rakahs until they returned to Madinah."
"20113","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a march, so they camped late at night, and they slept past the dawn prayer, and did not wake until the sun rose. When it rose high and spread, he ordered a man, so he called the adhan, then they prayed the two rakahs. When the time of the prayer came, they prayed."
"20114","Ismail narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So-and-so does not break fast in the daytime ever. He said: He has neither broken fast nor fasted."
"20115","Ismail narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon prayer, and when he gave salam he said: Which of you recited Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man from the people said: I did. He said: I knew that one of you was disputing it with me."
"20116","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu al-Dahma, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever hears of the Dajjal, let him keep away from him, for a man comes to him thinking he is a believer, then he keeps with him because of what he has of doubts until he follows him."
"20117","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accept the glad tidings, O Banu Tamim. He said: They said: You have given us tidings, so give us. He said: Accept the glad tidings, O people of Yemen. He said: We said: We have accepted, so inform us about the beginning of this matter, how was it? He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, was before everything, and His Throne was upon the water, and He wrote in the Tablet the mention of everything. He said: And one came to me and said: O Imran, your she-camel has slipped from its hobble. He said: So I went out, and the mirage was breaking between me and her. He said: So I went out after her, and I do not know what happened after me."
"20118","Ismail narrated to us, Yunus informed us, who said: I was informed that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah came to al-Hasan and said: A slave boy of mine fled, so I vowed that if I saw him I would cut his hand. He has come, and he is now at the bridge. He said: Al-Hasan said to him: Do not cut his hand. And he narrated to him that a man said to Imran ibn Husayn: A slave of mine fled, and I vowed that if I saw him I would cut his hand. He said: So do not cut his hand, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us, or he said: stand among us, and order us to give charity and forbid us mutilation."
"20119","Ismail narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Conquest, so he stayed in Makkah eighteen nights, praying only two rakahs, then saying to the people of the town: Pray four, for we are travelers."
"20120","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed two men from the Muslims for a man from the polytheists from Banu Uqayl."
"20121","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, that Ziyad appointed al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari over Khurasan. He said: Imran kept wishing to meet him, so he met him at the door and said: It used to please me to meet you. Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah? Al-Hakam said: Yes. He said: So Imran, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said takbir."
"20122","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from a man, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: I prayed behind Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, a prayer that reminded me of a prayer I had prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the two caliphs. He said: So I went and prayed with him, and he would say takbir whenever he prostrated and whenever he raised his head from prostration. So I said: O Abu Nujayd, who was the first to leave it? He said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, when he grew old and his voice weakened, he left it."
"20123","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him or to another: Did you fast the sirar of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, or when the people break fast, then fast two days."
"20124","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There was a woman captured by the enemy, and they used to rest their camels in the evening. She came to the camels seeking a camel to ride. Whenever she drew near a camel it growled, so she left it, until she came to a she-camel among them that did not growl. So she rode on it, then escaped, and reached Madinah. When the people saw her they said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Adba. She said: I vowed to slaughter it if Allah, Mighty and Majestic, saved me on it. He said: Evil is what you rewarded it: there is no vow for the son of Adam in what he does not own, and no vow in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"20125","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Judan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, then: O people, fear your Lord, indeed the earthquake of the Hour - a word fell upon my father - his mount stopped, the people stopped. He said: Do you know which day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. A word fell upon my father, saying: O Adam, send forth the delegation of Hell. He said: And what is the delegation of Hell? He said: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety to Hell. He said: So they wept. He said: Draw near and be straight. You are among the nations only like the mark. I hope that you are a quarter of the people of Paradise. I hope that you are a third of the people of Paradise."
"20126","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, or from a man, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: He passed by a man reciting to people, and when he finished he asked. So Imran said: Indeed to Allah we belong and to Him we return. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever recites the Quran, let him ask Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by it, for there will come people who recite the Quran asking people by it."
"20127","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: People from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Receive glad tidings, O Banu Tamim. They said: You have given us tidings, so give us. He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) almost changed. He said: Then people from the people of Yemen came, so he said to them: Accept the glad tidings since Banu Tamim did not accept it. They said: We have accepted."
"20128","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Said, from Husayn al-Muallim, who said: And I heard it from Husayn, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: I was a man with many illnesses, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about my prayer sitting. He said: Your prayer sitting is half of your prayer standing, and the prayer of a man lying down is half of his prayer sitting."
"20129","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr informed us, from his father, from a man, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"20130","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan ibn Hilal ibn Abi Zaynab narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa al-Qushayri, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon prayer, and when he finished he said: Which of you recited Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? One of the people said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I knew that one of you was disputing it with me."
"20131","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the death of al-Najashi reached him, said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him. So he stood and prayed over him, and the people were behind him."
"20132","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A brother of yours has died, so stand and pray over him, meaning al-Najashi."
"20133","Ismail narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So-and-so does not break fast in the daytime. He said: He has neither broken fast nor fasted."
"20134","Ismail narrated to us, Abu Harun al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Mutarrif, who said: Imran ibn Husayn said to me: O Mutarrif, by Allah, I used to think that if I wished I could narrate from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two consecutive days without repeating a hadith. Then what has made me slow in that and dislike it is that men from the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from some of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I witnessed as they witnessed and heard as they heard, narrate hadiths that are not as they say. And I knew that they do not fall short of good, so I fear that it may be confused to me as it was confused to them. Sometimes he would say: If I narrated to you that I heard from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) such and such, I would see that I had told the truth. And sometimes he would resolve and say: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say such and such."
"20135","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to me, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Ghanawi, who said: Hani al-Awar narrated to me, from Mutarrif, from Imran, he is Ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to this hadith. So I narrated it to my father, may Allah have mercy on him, and he approved it and said: He added in it a man."
"20136","Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Thaqif were allies of Banu Uqayl. Thaqif captured two men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) captured a man from Banu Uqayl, and al-Adba was taken with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was in bonds. He said: O Muhammad, O Muhammad. He said: What is your matter? He said: For what did you take me, for what did you take the foremost camel of the pilgrims, magnifying that. He said: I took you for the crime of your allies Thaqif. Then he turned away from him. He said: O Muhammad, O Muhammad, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was merciful, gentle, so he came to him and said: What is your matter? He said: I am a Muslim. He said: If you had said it while you controlled your affair, you would have prospered with complete prosperity. Then he turned away from him. He called him: O Muhammad, O Muhammad. So he came to him and said: What is your matter? He said: I am hungry, so feed me, and thirsty, so give me drink. He said: This is your need. He said: So he was ransomed for the two men. And a woman from the Ansar was captured, and al-Adba was taken with her. The woman was in bonds, then she slipped away one night from the bonds and came to the camels. Whenever she drew near a camel it growled, so she left it, until she reached al-Adba, and it did not growl. He said: And it was a trained she-camel. So she sat in its rear, then urged it, so it went. They were warned of her, so they sought her but she outstripped them. She vowed that if Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saved her on it, she would slaughter it. When she reached Madinah, the people saw her and said: Al-Adba, the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I vowed that if Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saved her on it, she would slaughter it. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Glory be to Allah, evil is what she rewarded it: if Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saved her, she would slaughter it. There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, and no vow in what the servant does not own."
"20137","Ismail narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, who said: Imran said to me: I narrate to you the hadith today so that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, may benefit you by it after today. Know that the best of the servants of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, on the Day of Resurrection are the much-praising. And know that there will always be a group from the people of Islam fighting upon the truth, dominant over those who oppose them, until they fight the Dajjal. And know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah from his family in the ten, and no verse was revealed abrogating that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it until he passed away. Each man then held the view that Allah willed him to hold."
"20138","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu al-Ala, who said: I think, from Mutarrif, from Imran, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him or to another: Did you fast the sirar of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, or when the people break fast, then fast two days."
"20139","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, who said: Abu Raja narrated to me, who said: Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People come out of Hell by the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they are named the Jahannamis."
"20140","Yahya narrated to us, from Awf, Abu Raja narrated to us, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, who said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we traveled by night until, when we were at the end of the night, we fell into that sleep, and no sleep is sweeter to the traveler than it. He said: Nothing woke us but the heat of the sun. The first to wake was so-and-so, then so-and-so, Abu Raja used to name them and Awf forgot them, then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, the fourth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he slept, we would not wake him until he woke by himself, because we did not know what happens, or occurs to him, in his sleep. When Umar woke and saw what had befallen the people, and he was a stout strong man, he said: So he said takbir and raised his voice with takbir, and kept saying takbir and raising his voice with takbir until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke at his voice. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke, they complained to him what had befallen them. He said: No harm, or: it does no harm. Move on. So they moved on and traveled a short distance, then camped. He called for ablution water and performed ablution, and the call to prayer was made, and he prayed with the people. When he finished his prayer, he saw a man apart who had not prayed with the people. He said: What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people? He said: O Messenger of Allah, major impurity befell me and there is no water. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You must use the earth, for it suffices you. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled, and the people complained to him of thirst. So he camped and called so-and-so, Abu Raja used to name him and Awf forgot him, and called Ali, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and said: Go and seek water for us. He said: They went and met a woman between two waterskins, or two sheets of water, on a camel of hers. They said to her: Where is the water? She said: My last contact with water was yesterday at this hour, and our people are absent. He said: They said to her: Then come along. She said: To where? They said: To the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: This one who is called the Sabian? They said: He is whom you mean, so come along. So they brought her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and told him the story. They made her dismount from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel and poured into it from the mouths of the two waterskins, or the two sheets, and tied their mouths, and opened the outlets, and it was called among the people: Give drink and draw water. So whoever wished drank and whoever wished drew water. The last of that was that he gave the one whom major impurity had befallen a vessel of water and said: Go and pour it over yourself. He said: She was standing looking at what was done with her water. He said: By Allah, it was taken from her, and it seemed to us that it was fuller than when he began with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather for her. So they gathered for her from dates, flour and sawiq, until they gathered much food for her, and put it in a cloth, and carried her on her camel, and placed the cloth before her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Know, by Allah, we have not diminished your water at all, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the One who gave us drink. He said: She came to her family, having been detained from them. They said: What detained you, O so-and-so? She said: Wonder: two men met me and took me to this one who is called the Sabian, and he did with my water such and such, of what happened. By Allah, he is either the most sorcerous of those between this and this, she said with her middle and index fingers, raising them to the sky, meaning the heaven and the earth, or he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in truth. He said: The Muslims afterwards used to raid what was around her of the polytheists, but did not harm the group she was in. She said one day to her people: I do not see these people leaving you deliberately, so do you desire Islam? They obeyed her and entered Islam."
"20141","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of a man sitting. He said: Whoever prays standing, it is better. The prayer of a man sitting is half of his prayer standing, and his prayer sleeping is half of his prayer sitting."
"20142","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man bit the hand of a man, so he pulled his hand, and his front tooth or his two front teeth fell out. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: One of you bites his brother as the stallion bites. There is no blood-money for you."
"20143","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while on one of his journeys, when the pace differed among his companions, raising his voice with these two verses: O people, fear your Lord, indeed the earthquake of the Hour is a great thing, the Day you see it, every nursing mother will forget, until he reached the end of the two verses. He said: When his companions heard that, they urged the mounts and knew he was about to say a saying. When they gathered around him, he said: Do you know which day that is? He said: That is the day Adam will be called, and his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will call him: O Adam, send forth a delegation to Hell. He will say: O Lord, what is the delegation of Hell? He said: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine in Hell and one in Paradise. He said: His companions became silent, so that they did not show a laugh. When he saw that, he said: Act and receive glad tidings. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations: they were never with anything but they made it numerous: Yajuj and Majuj, and those who perished from the sons of Adam and the sons of Iblis. He said: So it was relieved from them. Then he said: Act and receive glad tidings. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among people only like the mole on the side of the camel, or the mark on the foreleg of the beast."
"20144","Rawh narrated to us, Said and Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: So it was relieved from the people, and he said: except they made it numerous."
"20145","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, that Imran ibn Husayn narrated to him that a pregnant woman from Juhaynah was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for adultery. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it on me. He said: So he called her guardian and said: Treat her well, and when she gives birth then bring her to me. He did so, then he ordered regarding her, so her clothes were tied over her, then he ordered her, so she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said: You pray over her though she committed adultery? He said: She has repented a repentance which, if divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, would encompass them. And have you found better than that she gave herself generously for Allah, Mighty and Majestic?"
"20146","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Mirayah, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah, the Exalted."
"20147","Yahya narrated to us, Khalid ibn Rabah narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar, who said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Modesty is all good."
"20148","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Jamrah narrated to me, Zahdam ibn Mudarrib narrated to me, who said: I heard Imran ibn Husayn say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. I do not know whether twice or three times. Then there will come, or will come after you, people who vow but do not fulfill, and betray and are not trusted, and testify without being asked to testify, and obesity spreads among them."
"20149","Yahya narrated to us, Imran al-Qasir narrated to us, Abu Raja narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The verse of mutah was revealed in the Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and we acted by it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no verse was revealed abrogating it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it until he died."
"20150","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, informed us, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqyah except for an evil eye or a sting."
"20151","Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Samurah ibn Jundub and Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us with a sermon except that he ordered us to give charity and forbade us mutilation."
"20152","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A group from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Receive glad tidings. They said: You have given us tidings, so give us. He said: Then a tribe from Yemen came to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accept the glad tidings since Banu Tamim did not accept it."
"20153","Waki narrated to us, Jafar ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The begging of the rich is a disgrace on his face."
"20154","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever swears a false oath, solemn, deliberately, let him take with his face his seat from Hell."
"20155","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand from my nation enter Paradise without reckoning, who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqyah, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. He said: Ukkashah stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to make me among them. He said: You are among them. He said: Another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: Ukkashah has preceded you to it."
"20156","Yazid narrated to us, Khalid ibn Rabah Abu al-Fadl informed us, Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi narrated to us, Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Modesty is all good. A man from the tribe said: It is said in wisdom that some of it is dignity for Allah and some of it is weakness. Imran said to him: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you narrate to me from the scriptures."
"20157","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam, meaning Ibn Yahya, informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son died, so what is for me of his inheritance? He said: For you is the sixth. When he turned away, he called him and said: For you is another sixth. When he turned away, he called him and said: The other sixth is additional food."
"20158","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abu al-Tayyah al-Dubai, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women."
"20159","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, who said: I was walking with Imran ibn Husayn, one of us holding the hand of his companion, when we passed a beggar reciting the Quran. Imran held me back and said: Stand, let us listen to the Quran. When he finished, he asked. Imran said: Let us go. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite the Quran and ask Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by it, for after you there are people who recite the Quran asking people by it."
"20160","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Subayh, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin say: They mentioned before Imran ibn Husayn that the dead is punished by the weeping of the living. They said: How is the dead punished by the weeping of the living? Imran said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it."
"20161","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Imran ibn Isam, that an old man from the people of Basrah narrated to him, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about shaf and watr, so he said: It is the prayer, some of it even and some of it odd."
"20162","Abu Kamil and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always be a group from my nation fighting upon the truth, dominant over those who oppose them, until the last of them fights the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"20163","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Hassan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate to us most of the night about the Children of Israel, not standing except for the great prayer."
"20164","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned."
"20165","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned."
"20166","Ali narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate to us about the Children of Israel until morning, not standing in it except for the great prayer."
"20167","Ali narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Awn, he is al-Uqayli, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Most of the supplication of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, forgive me what I erred, what I did deliberately, what I concealed, what I declared, what I was ignorant of, and what I did deliberately."
"20168","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pregnant from adultery. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it on me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well, and when she delivers her load then bring her to me. He did so, then he ordered regarding her, so her clothes were tied over her, then he ordered her, so she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said to him: You pray over her though you stoned her? He said: She has repented a repentance which, if divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, would encompass them. And have you found better than that she gave herself generously for Allah, Mighty and Majestic?"
"20169","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, who said: Imran ibn Husayn came to his wife from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: It is not the time for hadith. She angered him. He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people were the poor. And I looked into Hell and saw most of its people were women."
"20170","Abd al-Razzaq and Affan narrated to us, the meaning, and this is the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq, both said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: Yazid al-Rishk narrated to me, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and appointed over them Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. He did something new on his journey, so he pledged, Affan said: four from the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed to mention his matter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Imran said: When we came from a journey, we began with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. He said: They entered upon him, and a man among them stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. So he turned away from him. Then the second stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. So he turned away from him. Then the third stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. So he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the fourth, his face changed, and said: Leave Ali, leave Ali. Ali is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me."
"20171","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plunders plunder is not from us."
"20172","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqyah except for an evil eye or a sting."
"20173","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a slave boy of poor people cut the ear of a slave boy of rich people. His family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, we are poor people. So he did not impose anything on him."
"20174","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, so he freed two and kept four in slavery. Muhammad ibn Sirin said: Had it not reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, I would have made it my own opinion."
"20175","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that he said: We performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid us it after that, nor did a prohibition about it come down from Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"20176","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Fudayl ibn Faddalah, a man from Qays, Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to us, who said: Imran ibn Husayn came out to us wearing a cloak of silk-wool blend which we had not seen on him before or after. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah, Mighty and Majestic, bestows a blessing upon, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves to see the trace of His blessing on His creation. And Rawh said in Baghdad: He loves to see the trace of His blessing on His servant."
"20177","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, who said: Qatadah was asked about shaf and watr, so he said: Imran ibn Isam al-Dubai narrated to us, from an old man from the people of Basrah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the prayer, some of it even and some of it odd."
"20178","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit informed us, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, who said: I went early to Imran ibn Husayn one day, so he said: O Abu al-Aswad, and he mentioned the hadith, that a man from Juhaynah or from Muzaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what people do today and strive in, is it decreed upon them, or passed upon them in a predestination that preceded, or in what they face of what their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought them and the proof was taken upon them by it? He said: Rather it is decreed upon them and passed upon them. He said: Then why do they act, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whoever Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created for one of the two abodes, He prepares him for its work. The confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: By the soul and Him who proportioned it, then inspired it its wickedness and its piety."
"20179","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, who said: And al-Sumayt al-Shaybani narrated to me, from Abu al-Ala, who said: A man from the tribe narrated to me that Imran ibn Husayn narrated to him that Ubays, or Ibn Ubays, among people from Banu Jusham, came to him. One of them said to him: Will you not fight so that there is no fitnah? He said: Perhaps I have fought until there was no fitnah. He said: Shall I not narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and I do not think it will benefit you, so listen. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Raid Banu so-and-so with so-and-so. He said: The men were lined, and the women were behind the men. Then when they returned, a man said: O Prophet of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, may Allah forgive you. He said: Did you do something new? He said: When the people were defeated, I found a man between the people and the women. He said: I am a Muslim, or he said: I submitted, so I killed him. He said: As seeking refuge by that when the spear overcame him? He said: Did you split his heart to look at it? He said: No, by Allah, I did not do it. So he did not seek forgiveness for him, or as he said. And he said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Raid Banu so-and-so with so-and-so. A man from my close kin went with them. When he returned to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Prophet of Allah, seek forgiveness of Allah for me, may Allah forgive you. He said: And did you do something new? He said: When the people were defeated, I caught two men between the people and the women. They said: We are Muslims, or they said: We submitted, so I killed them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What I fight people for is only for Islam. By Allah, I will not seek forgiveness for you, or as he said. He died afterwards, so his clan buried him, and in the morning the earth had cast him out. Then they buried him and guarded him a second time, and the earth cast him out. Then they said: Perhaps someone came while you were asleep and took him out. So they buried him a third time, then guarded him, and the earth cast him out a third time. When they saw that, they threw him, or as he said."
"20180","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: A man freed six slaves of his at his death. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, so he freed two of them."
"20181","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never stood among us as a preacher except that he ordered us to give charity and forbade us mutilation. He said: He said: Indeed among mutilation is that a man vows to cut his nose."
"20182","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: We performed tamattu in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not forbid us it, nor did a prohibition about it come down."
"20183","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so stand and pray over him. He said: So we lined up and prayed over him as you pray over the dead."
"20184","Affan narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so stand and pray over him. He said: So we stood and lined up over him as we line up over the dead, and prayed over him as we pray over the dead."
"20185","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hajib ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn al-Araj narrated to us, that Imran ibn Husayn said: I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20186","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, that Imran ibn Husayn said: He passed by a storyteller who recited then asked, so he said: Indeed to Allah we belong and to Him we return, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever recites the Quran, let him ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, by it, for there will come people who recite the Quran asking people by it."
"20187","Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"20188","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam, and whoever plunders is not from us."
"20189","Hashim and Affan narrated to us, both said: Mahdi narrated to us, Affan said: Ghaylan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), either he said it to Imran or to a man while he heard: Did you fast the surar of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, then fast two days."
"20190","Muhammad ibn Kathir, brother of Sulayman ibn Kathir, narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Imran, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you. So he returned it to him, then he sat, and he said: Ten. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. So he returned it to him, then he sat, and he said: Twenty. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. So he returned it to him, then he sat, and he said: Thirty."
"20191","Hawdhah narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Raja, mursal, and others said likewise."
"20192","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, Imran ibn Husayn informed me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered charity and forbade mutilation."
"20193","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, who said: A man was brought who freed six slaves at his death, and he had no wealth other than them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, so he freed two and kept four in slavery."
"20194","Sulayman ibn Harb and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif, who said: I prayed, I and Imran, behind Ali ibn Abi Talib. When he prostrated he said takbir, when he raised he said takbir, and when he rose from the two rakahs he said takbir. When we finished, Imran ibn al-Husayn took my hand and said: This one has prayed with us like the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: This one has reminded me of the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20195","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Bahz said: from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. He said: And Allah knows whether he mentioned the third or not. Then there will arise people who testify without being asked to testify, vow but do not fulfill, betray and are not trusted, and obesity spreads among them."
"20196","Affan narrated to us, Aban, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: I have incurred a hadd, so establish it on me, and she was pregnant. He ordered regarding her that she be treated well until she gives birth. When she gave birth, she was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered regarding her, so her clothes were tied over her, then he stoned her, then he prayed over her. Umar said: O Prophet of Allah, you pray over her though she committed adultery? He said: She has repented a repentance which, if divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, would encompass them. And have you found better than that she gave herself generously for Allah, Blessed and Exalted?"
"20197","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me that a man narrated to him that he asked Imran ibn Husayn about a man who vowed not to attend prayer in a mosque. Imran said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"20198","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, my father narrated to me that he met a man in Makkah, who narrated to him from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"20199","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us that Imran ibn Husayn narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good. Bushayr ibn Kab said: Some of it is weakness. Imran became angry and said: I do not see me narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Modesty is all good, while you say: Some of it is weakness. He said: So he shunned him and wanted not to narrate to him. It was said to him: He is as you like."
"20200","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20201","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd who said: I heard Abu Nadrah say: Imran ibn Husayn passed by our mosque, so I stood up to him and took hold of his bridle and asked him about prayer while traveling, so he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Hajj, and he would pray two rakahs until he passed away, and Abu Bakr two rakahs until he passed away, and Umar two rakahs until he passed away, and Uthman six or eight years, then he completed the prayer at Mina as four."
"20202","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Muhallab from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr three rakahs then gave salam, then a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called al-Khirbaq said: Has the prayer been shortened? So he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was as he said. He said: So he prayed one rakah then gave salam, then prostrated two prostrations then gave salam."
"20203","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah who said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa narrating from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, and a man began reciting behind him: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, so when he finished he said: Which of you recited, or which of you is the reciter? A man said: I did. He said: I thought that some of you was contesting it with me."
"20204","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar from Ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"20205","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him."
"20206","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, and Rawh said: Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn who said: We traveled by night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when it was the end of the night we camped and did not wake until the heat of the sun woke us, and a man among us would get up bewildered to his purification. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to be calm, then we departed and traveled until when the sun rose he performed wudu, then ordered Bilal and he called the adhan, then he prayed the two rakahs before Fajr, then the iqamah was made and we prayed. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not repeat it in its time tomorrow? He said: Does your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, forbid you from usury and accept it from you?"
"20207","Muawiyah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham who said: Al-Hasan claimed that Imran ibn Husayn narrated to him, he said: We traveled by night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, then he mentioned the hadith."
"20208","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand from my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment: they do not cauterize, nor seek ruqyah, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"20209","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever swears a false binding oath, let him take with his face his seat in the Fire."
"20210","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal from Abu Dahma al-Adawi from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears of the Dajjal, let him stay away from him, three times he says it, for a man will come to him following him while thinking him truthful due to the doubts sent with him."
"20211","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, a man informed us, and the man was named in the book of Abu Abd al-Rahman as Amr ibn Ubayd, he said: Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never became satiated with wheat bread with condiment until he passed away (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father, may Allah have mercy on him, had struck through this hadith in his book, so I asked him and he narrated it to me, and he wrote upon it: sahh sahh. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father only struck through this hadith because he was not pleased with the man from whom Yazid narrated."
"20212","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you fast anything of the sirar of this month? He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you break fast from Ramadan, then fast two days in its place."
"20213","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir from Imran ibn Husayn, Sulayman said: And I doubt regarding Imran, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Imran, did you fast anything of the surar of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, then fast two days in its place. And Ibn Abi Adi said: sirar."
"20214","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Naamah al-Adawi informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal from Bushayr ibn Kab from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good. Bushayr said: So I said: Among it is weakness and among it is incapacity. He said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you bring me insinuations; I will not narrate to you a hadith as long as I know you. They said: O Abu Nujayd, he is good-natured, and he is, and he is, and they kept at him until he calmed down and narrated."
"20215","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, and Affan and Abd al-Samad said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, Affan said in his hadith: Imran ibn Isam al-Dubai narrated to me, and Yazid said: from Qatadah from Imran ibn Isam al-Dubai from a shaykh of the people of Basra from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: By the even and the odd, he said: They are prayer; among it is even and among it is odd."
"20216","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah from Imran ibn Husayn that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of one sitting, he said: Whoever prays standing, it is better, and whoever prays sitting, he has half the reward of one standing, and whoever prays lying, he has half the reward of one sitting."
"20217","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not ride purple, nor wear saffron-dyed clothes, nor wear a shirt hemmed with silk. He said: And al-Hasan gestured to the collar of his shirt, and said: Verily the perfume of men is scent with no color, and verily the perfume of women is color with no scent."
"20218","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Abu Naamah al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar mentioning from Imran ibn Husayn who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Modesty is all good, then he mentioned the hadith."
"20219","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Amash from Abu Dawud from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a right due upon a man, then whoever delays it, he has for each day charity."
"20220","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him or to another: Did you fast anything of the surar of Shaban? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, then fast two days."
"20221","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Jurayri from Abu al-Ala from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, except that he did not say two days."
"20222","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, Affan said: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, from Hafs al-Laythi from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam, wearing silk, and wearing gold rings."
"20223","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: I heard a man from Banu Layth say: I testify regarding Imran ibn Husayn that he narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hanatim, gold rings, and wearing silk."
"20224","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: And Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mutarrif from Imran that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into the Fire and most of its people were women, and I looked into Paradise and most of its people were the poor."
"20225","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, and Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, he said: Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, he said, and he was a man suffering from piles, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prayer with a man sitting, he said: Whoever prays standing, it is better, and whoever prays sitting, he has half the reward of one standing, and whoever prays lying, he has half the reward of one sitting."
"20226","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hajib ibn Umar Abu Khushaynah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn al-Araj narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand from my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. He said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: They are those who do not seek ruqyah, nor cauterize, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"20227","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No vow in disobedience of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"20228","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The least of the inhabitants of Paradise are women."
"20229","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam, and whoever plunders a plunder is not from us."
"20230","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn, and Said al-Jurayri from Abu al-Ala from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you fast anything of the surar of Shaban? He said: No. He said: When you break the fast of Ramadan, then fast two days. Al-Jurayri said: Fast one day."
"20231","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, so we cauterized and we did not succeed nor prosper."
"20232","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Musa and Affan narrated to us, they said: Abu Hilal informed us, Affan said: Qatadah informed us, and Hasan said: from Qatadah from Abu Hassan al-Araj from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would narrate to us most of his night about Banu Israil, not standing except for major prayer."
"20233","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and slept past Subh until the sun rose, so he woke and ordered and adhan was called, then he prayed two rakahs, then waited until it was high, then ordered and he stood and prayed."
"20234","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur from Ribi ibn Hirash from Imran ibn Husayn or another that Husayn or Hasin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Abd al-Muttalib was better for his people than you; he would feed them liver and hump, and you slaughter them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him what Allah willed him to say. He said to him: What do you command me to say? He said: Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and decree for me the most right of my affair. He said: So the man went and embraced Islam, then came and said: I came to you and you said to me: Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and decree for me the most right of my affair, so what do I say now? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me what I concealed and what I declared, and what I erred and what I intended, and what I knew and what I was ignorant of."
"20235","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Judan from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He ate food and walked in the markets, meaning the Dajjal."
"20236","Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafii narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I adjure by Allah a man who heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something about the grandfather. A man stood and said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving him a third. He said: With whom? He said: I do not know. He said: You did not know."
"20237","Hasan ibn Musa and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif who said: I prayed a prayer behind Ali ibn Abi Talib, I and Imran ibn Husayn, and when he prostrated he said takbir, and when he rose he said takbir, and when he stood from the two rakahs he said takbir. When he finished the prayer, Imran took my hand and said: This one has reminded me of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before, or he said: This one has prayed with us the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20238","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur, Humayd and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would preach to us, ordering us with charity and forbidding us from mutilation."
"20239","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash from Khaythamah, not in it from al-Hasan al-Basri, who said: Imran ibn Husayn passed by a man telling stories, so Imran said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite the Quran and ask Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by it, before there comes a people who ask people by it."
"20240","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Quran was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instituted the sunnahs, then he said: Follow us, for by Allah if you do not, you will go astray."
"20241","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd from Abu Qatadah al-Adawi who said: We entered upon Imran ibn Husayn among a group of Banu Adi, among us Bushayr ibn Kab, and Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good, or: Modesty is all good. Bushayr ibn Kab said: We find in some books, or he said wisdom, that among it is tranquility and dignity for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and among it is weakness. Imran repeated the hadith and Bushayr repeated his statement, until he mentioned that two or three times, so Imran became angry until his eyes reddened, and said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you object with hadith of books. He said: So we said: O Abu Nujayd, there is no harm in it and he is from us. We kept at it until he calmed."
"20242","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan who said: Imran ibn Husayn informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw on a mans upper arm a ring, I think he said of brass, and said: Woe to you, what is this? He said: From al-wahinah. He said: It only increases you in weakness; cast it off from you, for if you die while it is upon you, you will never succeed."
"20243","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani from Said ibn al-Musayyab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ayyub, Hisham and Habib from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Humayd, Yunus, Qatadah and Simak ibn Harb from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, having no wealth besides them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew lots among them, returned four to slavery and freed two."
"20244","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani from Said ibn al-Musayyab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ayyub, Hisham and Habib from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Humayd, Yunus, Qatadah and Simak ibn Harb from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, having no wealth besides them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew lots among them, returned four to slavery and freed two."
"20245","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani from Said ibn al-Musayyab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ayyub, Hisham and Habib from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Humayd, Yunus, Qatadah and Simak ibn Harb from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, having no wealth besides them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew lots among them, returned four to slavery and freed two."
"20246","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Malih al-Hudhali narrated to us, a man of the tribe narrated to me that Yala ibn Suhayl passed by Imran ibn Husayn, so he said to him: O Yala, was I not informed that you sold your house for one hundred thousand? He said: Yes, I sold it for one hundred thousand. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sells a knot of wealth, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will set upon it a destroyer that destroys it."
"20247","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plunders a plunder is not from us."
"20248","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, Affan said: Abu al-Tayyah informed us, from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, so we cauterized and did not succeed nor prosper, and Affan said: They did not succeed nor prosper."
"20249","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, that Abu Qilabah narrated to him that Abu al-Muhallab narrated to him that Imran ibn Husayn narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lined up and we lined up behind him, and he prayed over him, and we did not think the funeral but placed before him."
"20250","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Ghaylan narrated to us, from Mutarrif from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him, or asked a man while he was present: Did you fast anything of the surar of this month? He said: No. He said: When you break fast, then fast two days."
"20251","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned."
"20252","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Hilal narrating from Abu Qatadah from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"20253","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb from al-Hasan al-Basri from Imran ibn Husayn that a man freed at his death six slaves of his, so his heirs came from the Bedouins and informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what he did. He said: Did he do that? He said: Had we known, Allah willing, we would not have prayed over him. He said: So he drew lots among them, freed two of them and returned four to slavery."
"20254","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Husayn from al-Shabi from Imran ibn Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No ruqyah except from an eye or a venomous sting."
